1. d4 d5 2. c4 Bf5 3. cxd5 { [%csl Gd8][%cal Rd8d5,Rb1c3,Re2e4] } 3... Bxb1 (3... Qxd5 4. Nc3 { [%cal Ge2e4] }) 4. Qa4+ { The Queen as an insertion move benefits from a few advantages compared to without this zwischenzug. } 4... c6 { This prevents the black knight though to occupy it's favorite position. } { [%cal Rb8c6] } 5. Rxb1 Qxd5 { The Queen as intermediate move now protecrs the a2 pawn also, To drive it away with b5 is a mistake. This chapter explains why. } { [%cal Rb7b5] } 6. Nf3 b5 { [%cal Ga4a5,Ga4c2] } 7. Qc2 { Taking the free pawn is a mistake. Let's see what happens if we do. } { [%csl Rd5][%cal Gc2e4,Rd5a2] } 7... Qxa2 { Although white offered a pawn it has a very good compensation. The pawn on c6 will cause problems for black. This possibilities will increase if white is able to castle. } { [%cal Ge1g1,Gb1a1] } 8. e4 { Capturing the complete centre as compensation too. } { [%csl Re4,Bc2][%cal Ge4f5,Ge4e5,Ge4d5,Gd4e5,Gd4c5,Rg8f6,Be4c6,Bc2c8] } 8... e6 { When the black bishop arrives on b4 white get into trouble. So } { [%cal Gf8b4,Gc1d2,Ga2a5] } 9. Bd2 { To move bishop d2 immediately prevents black bishop to check and there is the treat of taking b5 with the white bishop on f1 } { [%cal Gf1b5,Gc2c8,Ge8e7,Gb1c1,Gd2g5,Ga2a6,Gc1c7] } 9... Be7 { This is blacks best move. } (9... Nf6 10. Bxb5 cxb5 (10... Kd7 11. Ne5+) 11. Qc8+ Ke7 12. Bb4#) 10. Bd3 (10. Bxb5 cxb5 11. Qc8+ Bd8 { [%csl Rd2][%cal Rd2a5,Ga2a5,Ga2b1] }) 10... Nf6 { This seems natural but there is another treat. } 11. O-O { [%cal Gb1a1] } 11... Qa6 12. Rbc1 { [%cal Gc1c6] } 12... h6 { [%csl Gh6] } (12... O-O 13. e5 { [%cal Gd3h7] }) 13. d5 exd5 (13... cxd5 14. Qc8+ Qxc8 (14... Bd8 15. Bxb5+ (15. Qxa6 Nxa6 16. Bxb5+) 15... Nfd7 16. Ne5 O-O 17. Nxd7) 15. Rxc8+ Kd7 (15... Bd8 16. Bxb5+ Ke7 (16... Nfd7 17. Bxd7+ Nxd7 18. Rxa8) 17. Bb4#) 16. Rxh8) (13... c5 14. d6 Bxd6 (14... Bd8 15. Qxc5 { [%cal Gd3b5] }) 15. e5) 14. e5 Nfd7 (14... Ne4 15. Bxe4 dxe4 16. Qxe4 O-O 17. Nd4 Re8 (17... Rd8 18. Nf5) 18. Bxh6 gxh6 19. e6) 15. Bf5 { [%cal Ge5e6] } (15. e6) 15... Nc5 16. Bb4 Nbd7 17. Bxd7+ Nxd7 *


